# This checkout's own Skill Manager home and the three agent homes beside it.
#
# They are created by git-integration-repo's scripts/bootstrap-home.sh and are
# never committed: a home is machine-local state (absolute paths in
# home.runtime.json, a pinned CLI, installed unit trees), and committing one
# would hand every other checkout this machine's paths.
#
# These live in the CONSTITUENT rather than in the integration parent's root
# .gitignore because they are this repository's own concern: `git-issue-workflow`
# is a standalone repo with its own remote, and an agent that clones it directly
# still needs `bootstrap-home.sh --root .` to be safe. INTEGRATION.md rule 2
# forbids the reverse — putting a PARENT-only concern inside a constituent —
# which is not what these are.
.skill-manager/
.claude/
.codex/
.gemini/
